  "request_id": "ollama-e176-residue-activation-alignment-20261002-r3",
  "title": "Remove E176 Ollama install exception, rebind MODEL_DIALOGUE dependency to xingcheng service, and align mandated activation states",
  "summary": "Three residue classes remain after executed amendments rev 235 (B154 retirement), rev 238 (sibling convergence), rev 242 (module_capability_registry retirement) and rev 243 (Ollama provider/fault-vocabulary/directory residue). (1) Edict E176 still carries EXCEPTION-2 granting Ollama runtime+download+model-store install rights at registered C-drive paths - the last live install exception for the retired service. (2) project_architecture_directory row MODEL_DIALOGUE still declares 'registered local model runtime' as a dependency, while the runtime consumes the independent xingcheng model service via toolbox_start_tool(xingcheng) and its ToolHost /v1 contract; local-model no longer appears on the service start path. (3) architecture_activation_states rows BLOCK_XINGCHENG and UNIT_ASSISTANT read current_state=mandated vs required_state=active, the only two mismatched rows in the table - required_state must stay 'mandated' until physical-root hosting, separate-host isolation, migration receipt and independent verification evidence exist (the directory's own logical_boundary text forbids counting an empty directory as activation evidence). B154 itself already reads as a pure retirement record (lifecycle retired, rule is the retirement clause), and all nine OLLAMA_* fault codes plus the PROJECT_GPTBRIDGE dependency field were already converged by the rev-243 amendment - this request covers the remainder only.",
  "requested_by": "decision-sovereign",
  "origin": "codex-vs-implementation convergence pass ordered by governor: clear the last live Ollama residue (E176 install exception), align MODEL_DIALOGUE registry dependency semantics with current runtime, and unify BLOCK_XINGCHENG/UNIT_ASSISTANT directory/activation state pending activation evidence",
  "problem": {
    "summary": "E176 still grants the retired Ollama lane an install exception; MODEL_DIALOGUE still names the retired local-model carrier as a dependency instead of the xingcheng service it actually uses; BLOCK_XINGCHENG/UNIT_ASSISTANT demand 'active' while their physical roots are registered-but-unimplemented intended targets, producing the only two state mismatches in architecture_activation_states.",
    "affected": [
      "edicts",
      "project_architecture_directory",
      "architecture_activation_states"
    ],
    "scope": "codex-text and registry convergence only; no file, binary or implementation change"
  },
